    {
      "id": "p0091-b004",
      "kind": "aside",
      "source": {
        "text": "I’ve seen long discussions on Japanese message boards about why some things say “you win” in English and other things say “you won”",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.7283978,
          0.2978571,
          0.8975083,
          0.3928571
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.7283978,
          0.2978571,
          0.8975083,
          0.3928571
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "我见过日本论坛长篇讨论：为什么有些作品的英文写“you win”，另一些却写“you won”？",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
