    {
      "id": "p0091-b009",
      "kind": "aside",
      "source": {
        "text": "You know how people avoid the licorice ones when eating jelly beans? The same thing happens in Japan, but with peppermint drops",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.7283978,
          0.6014286,
          0.8975083,
          0.6964286
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.7283978,
          0.6014286,
          0.8975083,
          0.6964286
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "你知道有人吃糖豆时会挑开甘草味的吗？日本也有类似的情况，只不过被挑开的是薄荷糖。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
      "layout": {
        "bbox": [
          0.7334915,
          0.6014286,
          0.8995458,
          0.7078571
        ],
        "font_size": 15.5,
        "line_height": 1.4838709677419355,
        "font_weight": 450,
        "background": "transparent",
        "text_align": "left"
      },
      "notes": "原图与截图保留；译文为待审校初稿。",
      "calibration": {
        "bbox": [
          0.7334915,
          0.6014286,
          0.8995458,
          0.7078571
        ],
        "font_size": 15.5,
        "leading": 23.0
      },
      "annotations": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0091-b010",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "“Monster Candy” is available for free in the ruins. In English, this candy is described as having a “distinct, non-licorice” flavor. Licorice candy is popular in Western countries, but its striking flavor is also quite polarizing – some people love it, and some people despise it with a burning passion.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.0835365,
          0.7478571,
          0.7090418,
          0.8221429
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.0835365,
          0.7478571,
          0.7090418,
          0.8221429
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "在遗迹里可以免费拿到 Monster Candy（怪物糖果）。英文说明写它有一种“distinct, non-licorice”（独特、并非甘草味）风味。甘草糖在西方国家很受欢迎，但那强烈的味道也让人爱憎分明：有人爱不释口，有人则深恶痛绝。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
      "layout": {
        "bbox": [
          0.09372391266976103,
          0.745,
          0.7059855595667869,
          0.8292857142857143
        ],
        "font_size": 20,
        "line_height": 1.45,
        "font_weight": 450,
        "background": "transparent",
        "text_align": "justify"
      },
      "notes": "原图与截图保留；译文为待审校初稿。",
      "calibration": {
        "bbox": [
          0.09372391266976103,
          0.745,
          0.7059855595667869,
          0.8292857142857143
        ],
        "font_size": 20,
        "leading": 29.0
      },
      "annotations": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0091-b011",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Licorice candy isn’t as common in Japan, however, so the translator changed the candy to a different flavor: peppermint. Just like with licorice in the West, the peppermint flavor is highly divisive in Japan – some like it, and some would rather eat trash.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.0906677,
          0.8307143,
          0.7090418,
          0.9057143
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.0906677,
          0.8307143,
          0.7090418,
          0.9057143
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "不过，甘草糖在日本没那么常见，所以译者把说明中用来对比的口味换成了薄荷。就像西方的甘草味一样，日本人对薄荷味也很两极分化：有人喜欢，有人宁可去吃垃圾。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
      "layout": {
        "bbox": [
          0.09372391266976103,
          0.8385714285714285,
          0.7059855595667869,
          0.9142857142857143
        ],
        "font_size": 20,
        "line_height": 1.45,
        "font_weight": 450,
        "background": "transparent",
        "text_align": "justify"
      },
      "notes": "原图与截图保留；译文为待审校初稿。",
